WEBVTT

00:09.759 --> 00:13.179
DECEMBER 2020

00:14.264 --> 00:16.933
JINNAM BOXING

00:17.017 --> 00:19.019
[uptempo electronic music playing]

00:29.237 --> 00:30.113
[exhales sharply]

00:33.199 --> 00:34.325
[exhales deeply]

00:36.953 --> 00:37.871
[exhales]

00:44.627 --> 00:45.962
[grunts]

01:03.271 --> 01:04.856
[grunts, exhales]

01:07.400 --> 01:10.737
- [coughing]
- [sirens wailing]

01:15.658 --> 01:16.534
[groans]

01:26.628 --> 01:28.463
[driver] Oh, uh, sir.

01:28.546 --> 01:31.257
- You need to wear a mask on the bus, sir.
- [man mumbling]

01:31.341 --> 01:33.635
[driver] You can't ride the bus
without a mask. I'm sorry.

01:33.718 --> 01:34.594
[man] Let's go.

01:34.677 --> 01:36.638
[driver] You'll be allowed on
when you return with a mask.

01:36.721 --> 01:38.473
Who are you to tell me what to do?
[shouts]

01:38.556 --> 01:40.934
- [driver] We get penalized--
- [man 1] What? A mask?

01:42.185 --> 01:44.229
- It's my choice!
- Please leave, sir.

01:44.813 --> 01:47.190
[man] You're a driver,
so drive the damn bus.

01:47.273 --> 01:48.274
[driver] I'm telling you.

01:48.358 --> 01:51.528
- Please put on a mask and come back, sir.
- [man 1] You're just a driver. Come here!

01:52.070 --> 01:54.280
- [driver] There are passengers on board.
- [man 2] Please don't do this.

01:54.364 --> 01:56.574
- [man 1] What the hell is this? Whoa!
- [man 2] Whoa!

01:56.658 --> 01:58.785
- Sorry. Sorry.
- [man 1] Get off of me.

01:59.577 --> 02:01.037
What? Who the hell are you?

02:01.121 --> 02:03.623
[man 2] I'm sorry, I think
you'll have to walk home. Sorry.

02:03.706 --> 02:05.208
- [man 1 grunts]
- I'm sorry.

02:05.291 --> 02:07.335
[groans] You shi--

02:07.418 --> 02:09.212
- [man 2] Sorry, sir.
- [grunts, winces]

02:09.295 --> 02:11.214
- [man 2] I'm very sorry.
- [grunts]

02:11.297 --> 02:12.590
[man 2] Whoa, I'm sorry.

02:12.674 --> 02:14.467
- I hope you're not hurt. Sorry, sir.
- [man 1 wincing]

02:14.551 --> 02:15.885
[groans]

02:17.762 --> 02:19.264
Goddamn you little--

02:19.848 --> 02:20.849
I'm very sorry.

02:22.100 --> 02:23.226
Bullshit.

02:24.769 --> 02:26.938
- I'm really sorry.
- My ass.

02:29.649 --> 02:30.483
[man 1 groans]

02:31.192 --> 02:33.027
[man 2] Sorry about that. Thank you.

02:33.111 --> 02:34.863
- [driver] Thank you, sir.
- [man 2] No problem.

02:36.948 --> 02:40.076
[driver] See,
the passengers are grateful too.

02:43.913 --> 02:45.331
[gentle piano music playing]

02:50.420 --> 02:51.379
[crosswalk beeping]

02:59.304 --> 03:01.222
[man] The guy in the mask kept saying…

03:13.776 --> 03:14.694
[exhales]

03:18.781 --> 03:19.908
[keys jingling]

03:21.951 --> 03:23.661
[woman] I'm so sorry.

03:24.162 --> 03:27.707
God, I had no idea it would go on
for this long. [whimpers]

03:28.917 --> 03:31.169
I am so sorry that I have to ask you.

03:31.252 --> 03:32.086
I'm sorry.

03:32.170 --> 03:34.756
I'll try to put something together
next month. I promise.

03:35.840 --> 03:39.928
So, do you think can you wait
just one more month?

03:41.095 --> 03:42.972
I… I promise I'll pay you back.

03:43.806 --> 03:46.726
Yes, yes. Next month. I'll try my best.

03:47.310 --> 03:48.645
Yes, thank you.

03:50.396 --> 03:51.648
[door latches]

03:54.651 --> 03:55.610
[sighs]

04:00.490 --> 04:02.492
[theme music playing]

04:27.016 --> 04:30.895
BLOODHOUNDS

04:33.898 --> 04:35.900
Amidst the ongoing recession
brought on by COVID-19…

04:35.984 --> 04:37.986
CITIZENS TREMBLE WITH ANXIETY
ABOUT ABANDONED BUILDINGS IN THE CITY

04:38.069 --> 04:41.072
…a suspended building construction project
is threatening the safety of the citizens.

04:41.155 --> 04:42.115
NO TRESPASSING

04:42.156 --> 04:44.659
Construction on the building
you see behind me had been suspended twice

04:44.742 --> 04:47.370
due to on-site workers being diagnosed
with COVID-19.

04:47.453 --> 04:49.580
When the company went bankrupt,
the building was abandoned

04:49.664 --> 04:51.582
becoming an eyesore
in the middle of the city.

04:51.666 --> 04:54.335
Seoul City must act quickly
to resolve this situation.

04:54.836 --> 04:56.421
[gentle piano music playing]

05:02.051 --> 05:05.179
In the United States, over 3.5 million
hotel employees were laid off

05:05.263 --> 05:06.681
in the third quarter alone.

05:06.764 --> 05:08.808
I'm telling you
that for the next three to for years

05:08.891 --> 05:12.103
there will be no foreign companies
interested in acquiring this hotel.

05:12.603 --> 05:13.855
Domestic companies even less so.

05:13.938 --> 05:15.857
You make these claims
as though they're facts.

05:15.940 --> 05:17.817
I have a lot of friends
who are future leaders

05:17.900 --> 05:19.652
of Korea's top fifty corporations.

05:19.736 --> 05:22.363
I have thoroughly discussed it with them
and reached this conclusion,

05:22.447 --> 05:24.449
so these claims are highly likely
to be factual.

05:25.325 --> 05:26.159
Actually,

05:27.201 --> 05:28.536
they are simply facts.

05:29.245 --> 05:31.956
You'd be doing well to negotiate with me,
Mr. Vice President.

05:32.040 --> 05:32.915
Mr. Hong.

05:34.042 --> 05:37.628
As you know, our bank has already lent
400 billion won to this building.

05:37.712 --> 05:40.131
Stating you will only be paying back
300 isn't a negotiation.

05:40.214 --> 05:43.176
Shouldn't one be prepared to accept
some losses in the current situation?

05:43.760 --> 05:45.053
How else can business be done?

05:45.678 --> 05:48.681
I am not a businessman,
but I am the banker.

05:49.307 --> 05:51.809
Uh, Mr. Director, Mr. Vice President,

05:51.893 --> 05:53.811
the reason I brought the two of you
over here…

05:53.895 --> 05:54.729
[director] Yes.

05:54.812 --> 05:58.024
…is to push for a speedy completion
of the construction work on the building

05:58.107 --> 05:59.400
for the citizens' safety.

05:59.484 --> 06:01.361
Talking to him
is like talking to a brick wall.

06:01.444 --> 06:04.030
If you're suggesting
that I'm being unreasonable,

06:04.113 --> 06:06.699
let me ask you this,
which part of what you said is reasonable?

06:15.625 --> 06:17.710
I must apologize for my tardiness.

06:18.544 --> 06:21.714
This is Mr. Kim Myeong-gil.
I mentioned him before our meal.

06:22.215 --> 06:23.257
May I introduce you.

06:23.341 --> 06:26.344
Assemblyman Seo Woo-hyeon,
a close acquaintance of the mayor,

06:26.928 --> 06:28.596
introduced him to us.

06:29.430 --> 06:30.598
Kim Myeong-gil.

06:32.767 --> 06:34.852
KIM MYEONG-GIL

06:34.936 --> 06:35.770
[inhales]

06:35.853 --> 06:37.814
I'll contact you individually later today.

06:38.439 --> 06:39.273
Okay.

06:43.986 --> 06:44.862
Kim Myeong-gil.

06:55.748 --> 06:58.126
Excuse me,
but what kind of work do you do?

06:59.127 --> 07:00.878
Primarily I deal with investments.

07:00.962 --> 07:03.172
When good people request my assistance,

07:03.256 --> 07:05.550
I help them out
to the best of my abilities.

07:05.633 --> 07:08.052
So are you a moneylender?

07:08.136 --> 07:09.011
[chuckles]

07:09.095 --> 07:12.223
Hey, did you know
that this man's a loan shark?

07:13.099 --> 07:15.476
Mr. Kim dabbles in various lines of work.

07:15.560 --> 07:18.020
You really think this is the right place
to bring this predator?

07:20.398 --> 07:23.109
And you must be the eldest son
of Chairman Hong Woo-geun.

07:24.444 --> 07:27.447
When I was young, I worked for someone
named Chairman Bang in Myeong-dong.

07:28.239 --> 07:30.575
You wouldn't remember
since you were a baby at that time,

07:30.658 --> 07:32.785
but when the IMF crisis hit Korea,

07:32.869 --> 07:35.872
Iil Group nearly went bankrupt
because they didn't have six billion

07:35.955 --> 07:37.457
after fifty years in business.

07:37.999 --> 07:41.836
Back then, Chairman Hong Woo-geun
went to my boss, Chairman Bang,

07:41.919 --> 07:43.463
to ask for assistance.

07:43.546 --> 07:46.007
He got down on his knees
saying he had to save the company

07:46.090 --> 07:47.091
at whatever cost.

07:47.633 --> 07:50.678
And with all his sincerity
and his passion,

07:50.761 --> 07:51.762
he got to Chairman Bang.

07:53.097 --> 07:53.931
So then,

07:54.515 --> 07:56.601
I filled up a bag
with six billion in cash,

07:56.684 --> 07:57.852
and I went over to your house.

07:58.644 --> 08:02.482
I also remember your mother prepared
some refreshing Korean melon for me

08:02.565 --> 08:03.733
to express her gratitude.

08:05.067 --> 08:08.070
There is no dirty money
unless it's used for nefarious agendas,

08:08.154 --> 08:10.740
but when used for good,
that makes it good money.

08:11.324 --> 08:14.202
I came here
to extend what support I have to offer.

08:17.955 --> 08:20.458
How are the negotiations?

08:21.125 --> 08:23.878
There were differences
in the amount they had in mind.

08:23.961 --> 08:27.215
- So we were just talking.
- Ah… How much of discrepancy?

08:27.298 --> 08:28.466
A hundred billion.

08:28.966 --> 08:29.800
[scoffs]

08:32.678 --> 08:36.599
Mr. Hong, do you plan on overseeing
hotel operations yourself?

08:36.682 --> 08:39.435
I got my master's in hotel management
in Switzerland

08:39.936 --> 08:41.437
and worked for four years in Hong Kong.

08:41.521 --> 08:43.648
I see you are well-prepared.

08:45.233 --> 08:48.444
With your permission,
I would like to make an investment.

08:48.528 --> 08:51.239
[inhales deeply] What's your offer?

08:51.322 --> 08:55.785
Well… you need 100 billion,
so I'll invest that much.

08:59.330 --> 09:02.124
If need be, I will invest more.

09:02.208 --> 09:03.167
What are the terms?

09:03.251 --> 09:04.085
Right.

09:04.627 --> 09:05.920
There are only three.

09:06.462 --> 09:09.423
First off,
I would like to have a small casino

09:09.924 --> 09:12.176
built on the highest floor
of the hotel's structure.

09:12.260 --> 09:14.804
Just as you dream of managing a hotel,
Mr. Hong,

09:14.887 --> 09:17.431
well, I dream of operating my own casino.

09:18.432 --> 09:19.559
And secondly,

09:19.642 --> 09:23.563
I ask that you help me set up a small bar
in the basement of the hotel.

09:23.646 --> 09:25.231
The last thing is,

09:25.314 --> 09:27.358
if something like COVID-19
were to spread again,

09:27.441 --> 09:30.820
I would like our hotel
to be a quarantine space.

09:30.903 --> 09:33.614
for those without money,
and it will be free of charge.

09:34.490 --> 09:35.741
The harder the times get,

09:35.825 --> 09:38.494
the more we all should be looking out
for one another.

09:38.578 --> 09:41.747
Because… that's how we build
a better world.

09:46.043 --> 09:47.712
The 100 billion won investment

09:48.504 --> 09:50.715
can be available to you
as early as tomorrow.

09:52.008 --> 09:53.509
[ominous music playing]

10:06.689 --> 10:08.566
- [grunts]
- It went well?

10:09.984 --> 10:11.819
- Mm-hm.
- So they'll bite?

10:12.403 --> 10:15.740
- [scoffs] Mm.
- [laughs]

10:16.324 --> 10:17.158
[woman] Oh yay!

10:17.241 --> 10:20.286
So I guess I need to start thinking
about how I want to decorate the bar!

10:20.369 --> 10:22.913
Well, uh, people don't go to bars
to see how they're decorated.

10:22.997 --> 10:24.540
They go to see the girls.

10:24.624 --> 10:26.459
So you better get busy
hiring some pretty girls.

10:27.043 --> 10:29.128
No, I think you should get busy,
you fucker.

10:29.211 --> 10:32.214
You know, it would be better
if you could talk as nice as you look.

10:32.298 --> 10:34.133
What would you know? You prick!

10:34.634 --> 10:35.468
[exhales forcefully]

10:35.551 --> 10:37.053
- [woman laughs]
- [scoffs]

10:37.637 --> 10:39.013
I need to wipe my face.

10:39.597 --> 10:40.431
Oh.

10:41.766 --> 10:42.808
[Myeong-gil exhales deeply]

10:43.392 --> 10:44.226
Here you go.

10:49.315 --> 10:51.108
[ominous music playing]

10:59.742 --> 11:00.785
Let's get going.

11:05.206 --> 11:06.707
How's the Seongeun Building?

11:06.791 --> 11:10.002
None of the tenants have any ties
to the police or prosecutor's office.

11:10.086 --> 11:11.379
Did you also check in-laws?

11:11.462 --> 11:14.131
Yes, of course. I told you
I only overlooked it that one time.

11:14.215 --> 11:16.300
Someone could have a partner who's a cop.

11:16.801 --> 11:18.552
Do your job well
so he doesn't have to worry.

11:18.636 --> 11:20.513
Ah, why don't you worry about yourself?

11:21.013 --> 11:22.098
Jang-do,

11:23.265 --> 11:25.601
you should speak to my woman
with more respect.

11:26.894 --> 11:28.604
Yes, you're right. I'm sorry, sir.

11:28.688 --> 11:30.606
Hey, apologize to me, you asshole.

11:30.690 --> 11:31.565
[inhales sharply]

11:31.649 --> 11:33.734
This asshole apologizes to you, ma'am.

11:33.818 --> 11:36.487
[groans] Hurry up, please.
I could really use a drink.

11:36.570 --> 11:37.530
[Jang-do] Yes, sir.

11:39.865 --> 11:42.827
[commentator 1] This is the 2020 KBFC
Rookie of the Year Tournament.

11:42.910 --> 11:44.787
The Rookie of the Year Tournament
is supposed to be held

11:44.870 --> 11:48.290
amidst the loud shouting and cheering
of fans expressing their love and support,

11:48.374 --> 11:50.501
but due to COVID-19,
there are no spectators today.

11:50.584 --> 11:52.420
It feels rather gloomy in here,
don't you think?

11:52.503 --> 11:53.337
That's right.

11:53.421 --> 11:55.548
The Rookie of the Year tournament
is normally a rowdy affair

11:55.631 --> 11:56.841
with lots of cheering for everyone.

11:56.924 --> 11:58.134
- [coaches yelling]
- [bell dings]

11:58.217 --> 12:01.303
[commentator 1] As we speak, we begin
the third round of Hong Woo-jin's match.

12:01.387 --> 12:02.972
Now we have a middleweight match here

12:03.055 --> 12:04.598
with Hong Woo-jin in the red trunks,

12:04.682 --> 12:06.684
going up against Jung Jae-hun
in the blue trunks.

12:06.767 --> 12:07.601
[coach 1] Get in there.

12:07.685 --> 12:09.562
[commentator 2]
Great combination of body shots.

12:09.645 --> 12:11.897
[commentator 1] Now we see Hong Woo-jin
leaning against the ropes.

12:11.981 --> 12:13.983
[commentator 2] He provokes his opponent
after landing body shots.

12:14.066 --> 12:16.277
[commentator 1]
Would you look at that provocation.

12:16.360 --> 12:18.446
I mean, I wouldn't go near.

12:18.529 --> 12:20.239
Whoa, a body shot!

12:20.322 --> 12:22.450
- [coach cheers]
- [commentator 2] A clean hit to the body.

12:22.533 --> 12:24.285
[commentator 1]
He landed a blow to the face.

12:24.368 --> 12:26.537
He knocks his opponent down! Hong Woo-jin!

12:26.620 --> 12:29.039
[commentator 2] Whoa! A double right
followed by a one-two strike.

12:29.123 --> 12:31.959
[commentator 1] Look at that footwork.
He has great showmanship.

12:32.042 --> 12:33.294
[commentator 2] Whoa, it's a KO.

12:33.836 --> 12:34.795
KIM RAE-HYEON
KIM GUN-WOO

12:34.879 --> 12:37.465
[commentator 1] We have Kim Gun-woo
going up against Kim Rae-hyeon.

12:37.548 --> 12:40.050
Kim Gun-woo in blue, everybody,
the super rookie in blue trunks.

12:40.134 --> 12:43.512
[commentator 2] Kim Gun-woo is looking
for a chance with his guard up.

12:43.596 --> 12:45.556
- A body blow!
- [commentator 1] He goes to his knees!

12:45.639 --> 12:48.142
[commentator 2] That's right.
A precision blow to the solar plexus…

12:48.225 --> 12:50.186
- That's the end of the match.
- [commentator 2] Indeed.

12:50.269 --> 12:52.062
[commentator 1] Ending with just one blow.

12:52.146 --> 12:54.940
Kim Gun-woo mows down his opponent
with a single blow again.

12:55.024 --> 12:56.484
[commentator 2]
He's a matchless competitor.

12:56.567 --> 12:58.068
[commentator 1]
A terrifying rookie has emerged.

12:58.152 --> 13:00.446
[commentator 2]
Things are already getting heated.

13:00.529 --> 13:02.281
[commentator 1] He's getting cornered.

13:02.364 --> 13:05.159
[coaches shouting indistinctly]

13:05.242 --> 13:08.245
He grabs him and throws him over.
He threw his opponent down.

13:08.329 --> 13:09.872
[commentator 2]
That was against the rules.

13:09.955 --> 13:13.375
- He did it first.
- [commentator 2] He's too agitated now.

13:13.459 --> 13:15.461
- [referee] Box!
- [man] Let's do this!

13:15.544 --> 13:18.297
[commentator 1] He parts his hair.
Hong's showmanship is unmatched.

13:18.380 --> 13:20.257
[commentator 2]
That is Hong Woo-jin for you.

13:20.341 --> 13:21.884
[commentator 1] He provokes. He dodges.

13:21.967 --> 13:23.260
Wow! Look at him dodge!

13:23.761 --> 13:25.054
[boxers grunting]

13:25.721 --> 13:28.682
Here he goes again…
He connects! We have a knockdown!

13:28.766 --> 13:30.518
[commentator 2]
It's Hong Woo-jin's specialty.

13:30.601 --> 13:32.144
A double jab followed by a straight!

13:32.228 --> 13:33.979
[commentator 1] Hong Woo-jin, the marine.

13:34.063 --> 13:35.272
Hong Woo-jin advances again.

13:35.356 --> 13:36.398
HONG WOO-JIN

13:36.482 --> 13:37.441
[Gun-woo's coach] Go lower.

13:37.525 --> 13:39.860
[commentator 1] A match between
Kim Gun-woo and Lee Yong-gyu.

13:39.944 --> 13:41.529
[boxers grunting]

13:41.612 --> 13:44.365
Kim Gun-woo in the red trunks
is built like a tank.

13:44.448 --> 13:45.783
He dodges both blows.

13:45.866 --> 13:48.452
[commentator 2]
Kim Gun-woo's strength lies in infighting.

13:48.536 --> 13:51.372
He is leveraging his skills
in close-range hitting.

13:51.455 --> 13:53.541
[commentator 1]
Another punch, and he dodges.

13:53.624 --> 13:57.461
A body shot! He brings down his opponent
with one blow!

13:57.545 --> 13:59.088
[commentator 2] A left hook to the body.

13:59.171 --> 14:01.382
I had that level of talent
when I was a contender.

14:01.465 --> 14:03.551
- [Gun-woo] Are you all right?
- Yeah.

14:03.634 --> 14:06.053
[commentator 1]
That's why you won a gold medal.

14:06.804 --> 14:08.514
Now, Kim Gun-woo versus Hong Woo-jin.

14:08.597 --> 14:11.267
- Yeah, let's see.
- Let's find out who takes home the trophy.

14:11.350 --> 14:14.019
No big moves.
Short punches. Use your waist!

14:14.103 --> 14:16.856
Watch out for his left hook.
His punches are no joke.

14:23.737 --> 14:26.240
Bro, I'm a marine.

14:26.323 --> 14:27.157
THE STRONGEST

14:27.241 --> 14:28.492
Watch out for his left hook.

14:28.576 --> 14:30.911
And I'm telling you,
I'm an invincible marine.

14:30.995 --> 14:34.081
Okay, but don't cry
if you get the shit beat out of you.

14:34.164 --> 14:34.999
All right?

14:35.541 --> 14:36.375
[exhales deeply]

14:39.044 --> 14:40.838
- [coach 1] Let's go!
- [coach 2] You got this.

14:40.921 --> 14:41.755
Keep your hands up.

14:41.839 --> 14:43.549
- [referee] Come forward to meet.
- [grunts]

14:43.632 --> 14:45.801
Now good luck to you both.
To your corners.

14:49.972 --> 14:52.474
[commentator 1] His fighting up until now
has truly been a marvel.

14:52.558 --> 14:55.686
Kim Gun-woo, the super rookie,
has a very unique fighting style.

14:55.769 --> 14:57.897
[commentator 2] That's right.
Kim Gun-woo is an infighter

14:57.980 --> 14:59.440
that's good against other infighters.

14:59.523 --> 15:00.983
[commentator 1] Right.

15:01.066 --> 15:02.192
[commentator 2] On the other hand,

15:02.276 --> 15:05.654
Hong Woo-jin is an out-boxer
with a counter up his sleeve.

15:05.738 --> 15:07.948
[commentator 1] That's right.
Hong Woo-jin knows how to have fun

15:08.032 --> 15:09.116
during his matches.

15:09.199 --> 15:10.409
[commentator 1] On the other hand,

15:10.492 --> 15:13.037
we have his opponent
who stoically plays it by the book.

15:13.120 --> 15:15.831
He's going in! He's going!
He's cornering him!

15:15.915 --> 15:18.500
Can Hong Woo-jin get out?
Can he get out of this?

15:18.584 --> 15:20.669
Wow! He got out of that really well.

15:20.753 --> 15:23.547
[commentator 2]
Hong Woo-jin is just remarkably fast.

15:23.631 --> 15:26.425
And since Kim Gun-woo
is also a middleweight…

15:26.508 --> 15:28.636
[commentator 1] Wow,
he goes for a wild swing!

15:28.719 --> 15:31.055
Here we go. He guards the body shot.

15:31.138 --> 15:33.015
[commentator 2]
Kim Gun-woo has a great defense.

15:33.098 --> 15:35.351
- [commentator 1] Doesn't he?
- [commentator 2] He's like a rock.

15:35.434 --> 15:36.936
And he keeps on guarding.

15:37.019 --> 15:38.687
- [both grunting]
- [commentator 1] Uppercut!

15:38.771 --> 15:40.481
He landed that one.

15:40.564 --> 15:41.774
[commentator 2] Indeed he did.

15:41.857 --> 15:43.484
[commentator 1]
What a performance this is.

15:43.567 --> 15:45.945
A right hook! Wow, what a dodge.

15:46.028 --> 15:46.862
[Woo-jin grunting]

15:46.946 --> 15:50.074
Hong Woo-jin is
constantly applying nonstop pressure.

15:50.908 --> 15:53.327
- [commentator 2] Another left.
- [commentator 1] Can he recover?

15:53.410 --> 15:55.371
And Hong Woo-jin-- He goes down.

15:55.454 --> 15:57.623
- He's down!
- One… two…

15:57.706 --> 15:59.625
- Three… four
- [commentator 2] With stomach blows,

15:59.708 --> 16:01.085
the shock does not come right away.

16:01.168 --> 16:04.213
It takes around five seconds.
That is when it hits.

16:04.296 --> 16:06.256
- [Woo-jin groans]
- [referee] Six, seven…

16:06.340 --> 16:08.092
[commentator 1] He gets up
after five seconds.

16:08.175 --> 16:09.802
He recovered well from that one.

16:09.885 --> 16:10.803
Yes, he did.

16:10.886 --> 16:12.930
[commentator 2]
But that has definitely got to sting.

16:13.013 --> 16:15.307
[commentator 1]
There's going to be an aftereffect.

16:15.391 --> 16:16.433
[commentator 2] I think so.

16:17.226 --> 16:18.060
Come on.

16:18.143 --> 16:20.062
[rock music playing]

16:20.145 --> 16:23.565
Come on!

16:28.195 --> 16:29.279
[Woo-jin grunts]

16:30.197 --> 16:32.074
[music fades]

16:36.120 --> 16:36.996
[rock music resumes]

16:37.079 --> 16:40.040
[yelling]

16:41.583 --> 16:42.418
[exhales deeply]

16:48.173 --> 16:49.008
Come on.

16:49.717 --> 16:52.052
Hey… come get some.

16:53.721 --> 16:54.888
Son of a bitch.

16:57.891 --> 16:59.893
Come get me!

17:01.603 --> 17:03.105
[commentator 1] Will he take the bait?

17:03.188 --> 17:05.357
- Kim Gun-woo has a lot to think about.
- Come on!

17:05.441 --> 17:07.735
[commentator 1]
And there he goes! Will he connect?

17:07.818 --> 17:11.155
- Stop! One, two…
- [Woo-jin groaning]

17:11.238 --> 17:13.574
- Three… four…
- [Woo-jin whimpering]

17:13.657 --> 17:15.409
[commentator 1]
His tactics really backfired.

17:15.492 --> 17:16.326
[referee] KO!

17:16.410 --> 17:18.078
[commentator 1]
Kim Gun-woo went in for the kill

17:18.162 --> 17:21.790
and ended the match
once again with the same body shot.

17:21.874 --> 17:24.293
I'll tell you something.
That body shot is ruthless.

17:24.376 --> 17:26.587
- [sighs]
- [Woo-jin whimpering]

17:28.464 --> 17:29.590
You all right?

17:30.424 --> 17:32.843
I have tainted the honor
of my fellow marines.

17:33.427 --> 17:35.095
A blow to the liver will do that.

17:36.430 --> 17:37.639
Okay, I'm out of here.

17:38.474 --> 17:39.892
What about dinner, huh?

17:40.601 --> 17:41.810
There's the pandemic.

17:42.394 --> 17:44.104
I mean,
your boy has just gone through a lot.

17:44.188 --> 17:45.564
The least you can do is feed him.

18:01.455 --> 18:02.915
Go home and order in.

18:04.708 --> 18:05.542
[sighs]

18:06.126 --> 18:06.960
Later.

18:11.131 --> 18:12.674
[wincing]

18:16.303 --> 18:17.513
[exhales]

18:19.098 --> 18:19.973
Oh.

18:23.227 --> 18:24.853
What? Huh? What?

18:25.854 --> 18:26.855
Wanna grab a bite?

18:27.606 --> 18:29.274
Why would I wanna grab food with you?

18:29.858 --> 18:32.277
I was gonna get some pork belly.
Thought you might want some.

18:34.655 --> 18:35.531
[inhales sharply]

18:35.614 --> 18:36.573
Are you pitying me?

18:37.157 --> 18:37.991
No.

18:38.075 --> 18:40.202
Go ask those other assholes you KO'd
to eat with you.

18:40.285 --> 18:41.912
But they all went home.

18:43.122 --> 18:44.248
[sighs]

18:56.677 --> 18:58.804
- Wasn't the prize money ten million?
- Yeah.

19:00.264 --> 19:02.057
Then why settle for pork belly?

19:02.141 --> 19:03.392
Let's get rib eye.

19:03.475 --> 19:06.145
- I'm only going to spend 50,000.
- Why?

19:06.228 --> 19:07.980
I need to give the rest to my mom.

19:08.063 --> 19:10.107
- Do you owe your mom money?
- No.

19:10.190 --> 19:11.066
Then why?

19:11.567 --> 19:13.443
I have to pay the rent for her store.

19:14.319 --> 19:15.404
You're a good son.

19:16.196 --> 19:17.614
Just spend an extra 10,000.

19:17.698 --> 19:20.284
This barbecue buffet I know
charges 29,000 a person.

19:20.367 --> 19:22.035
It's insane, and they serve Korean beef.

19:22.119 --> 19:23.954
- You serious?
- Of course not, idiot.

19:24.454 --> 19:25.455
[Woo-jin scoffs]

19:25.539 --> 19:28.500
How could they afford
to serve Korean beef that cheap? [scoffs]

19:28.584 --> 19:30.377
Do you spend all your time working out?

19:31.461 --> 19:33.881
Anyway, that buffet is all right.
Just spend a little more.

19:33.964 --> 19:34.798
No.

19:35.924 --> 19:36.758
[sighs]

19:37.259 --> 19:38.093
Hey.

19:46.435 --> 19:47.978
[gentle instrumental music playing]

19:48.061 --> 19:48.896
Let's go.

19:50.480 --> 19:52.107
How is your left hook so strong?

19:52.983 --> 19:54.610
Back when I worked part-time
at a junkyard,

19:54.693 --> 19:56.028
I practiced my hooks on a tire.

19:56.111 --> 19:57.279
Just your left?

19:58.405 --> 19:59.781
Why would I only work on my left?

19:59.865 --> 20:01.867
No, I'm asking
if you only worked on your left.

20:01.950 --> 20:03.785
No, of course I hit with both hands.

20:03.869 --> 20:05.537
Then why is your left so strong?

20:05.621 --> 20:08.874
- Actually, my right is stronger.
- Then why use only your left?

20:08.957 --> 20:11.293
Because I couldn't find a good time
to use my right.

20:12.628 --> 20:13.545
What a show-off.

20:14.588 --> 20:15.422
You think so?

20:15.505 --> 20:17.674
You're saying you could take
everyone down with just your left.

20:18.258 --> 20:19.468
At least today, yes.

20:19.551 --> 20:21.386
Yeah, see? What a show-off.

20:21.970 --> 20:23.347
Actually, I consider myself humble.

20:23.430 --> 20:24.306
Flip the pork already.

20:24.389 --> 20:26.308
Not yet. It needs 30 more seconds.

20:26.391 --> 20:28.143
Well, I think it's ready now.

20:28.227 --> 20:30.229
You're wrong.
I worked part-time at a barbecue place.

20:30.312 --> 20:31.355
I know my meat.

20:31.438 --> 20:34.024
Damn, bro,
you've worked a lot of part-time jobs.

20:34.107 --> 20:35.525
- Are you poor?
- Mm-hm.

20:35.609 --> 20:37.069
My family lost everything.

20:39.488 --> 20:40.405
How?

20:41.490 --> 20:42.366
[clicks tongue]

20:42.866 --> 20:45.244
My dad was a researcher
for a large corporation.

20:45.327 --> 20:47.871
He sued them for wrongful termination
and ended up losing the suit.

20:47.955 --> 20:48.789
[sighs]

20:48.872 --> 20:51.250
Legal fees from back then all became debt.

20:52.251 --> 20:54.753
You can't beat the big companies.
The rich always come out on top.

20:54.836 --> 20:55.879
That's true.

20:58.590 --> 21:01.551
- What were your other gigs?
- Well, I dabbled in this and that.

21:01.635 --> 21:03.553
For the most part,
I made deliveries with my mom.

21:03.637 --> 21:04.638
[scoffs]

21:04.721 --> 21:06.265
I guess you're a world-class part-timer.

21:07.432 --> 21:08.267
[chuckles]

21:09.101 --> 21:10.435
Oh!

21:10.519 --> 21:13.021
You are good at everything.
You've led a good life.

21:13.563 --> 21:15.107
I see you grill with your right hand.

21:15.190 --> 21:16.149
[chuckles]

21:16.233 --> 21:17.567
So when did you start boxing?

21:18.277 --> 21:20.195
Uh, about three years ago.

21:20.279 --> 21:22.281
- After school?
- After my military service.

21:22.364 --> 21:23.532
Ah… [inhales sharply]

21:24.032 --> 21:26.285
I first put on my gloves
for the first time in sixth grade.

21:26.368 --> 21:27.995
My dad was on the national team.

21:28.078 --> 21:30.122
Wow, that's so cool.

21:30.205 --> 21:31.540
And so what's your father's name?

21:31.623 --> 21:32.499
Hong Seong-geun.

21:33.125 --> 21:34.501
Barcelona bronze medalist.

21:34.584 --> 21:36.169
- Oh.
- Know him?

21:36.253 --> 21:37.379
No.

21:38.463 --> 21:40.048
Most boxers seem to know him.

21:40.132 --> 21:42.134
Oh. Sorry.

21:43.593 --> 21:45.429
I assume
your dad taught you how to box, right?

21:46.138 --> 21:47.222
We aren't that close.

21:48.098 --> 21:48.932
Why?

21:49.433 --> 21:51.435
My dad is never satisfied
with anything that I do.

21:52.269 --> 21:54.062
He won his bronze medal at my age,

21:54.896 --> 21:57.107
so he judges me
based on his accomplishments.

21:57.607 --> 21:58.775
Hm. [clicks tongue]

21:59.526 --> 22:01.028
So you're basically saying

22:01.528 --> 22:03.363
that your dad won a bronze medal
at the Olympics

22:03.447 --> 22:04.948
when he was only twenty-five years old?

22:06.074 --> 22:07.617
No, twenty-seven.

22:10.746 --> 22:12.247
Oh, how old are you?

22:12.831 --> 22:14.041
Twenty-seven.

22:14.124 --> 22:15.208
[inhales sharply] Uh,

22:15.834 --> 22:18.879
I'm sorry, man. I'm actually twenty-five.
I'm sorry. Please forgive my manners.

22:18.962 --> 22:20.756
Ah, you ass!

22:20.839 --> 22:21.673
Please forgive me.

22:21.757 --> 22:22.799
- Hey.
- Yes?

22:22.883 --> 22:24.593
Learn to respect your elders, got it?

22:24.676 --> 22:25.927
- Yes.
- Understand?

22:26.470 --> 22:27.304
Sure.

22:27.971 --> 22:28.889
Flip it now.

22:28.972 --> 22:31.266
Oh, not yet.
It still needs one more minute.

22:31.350 --> 22:33.518
- I said to flip it.
- I can't do that.

22:33.602 --> 22:37.147
Oh god, you are one stubborn punk, bro.
You've served in the army?

22:37.230 --> 22:40.192
Yes, I told you earlier I started boxing
after I finished my military service.

22:40.275 --> 22:41.568
Yeah, you did.

22:41.651 --> 22:43.737
What I mean is,
where were you stationed, huh?

22:43.820 --> 22:45.072
- Oh.
- You need to learn to keep up.

22:45.155 --> 22:47.240
Um, yes, I was in the Marine Corps.

22:48.450 --> 22:51.161
Hey! I'm a marine too!

22:51.661 --> 22:52.579
Oh.

22:52.662 --> 22:53.663
What class?

22:53.747 --> 22:56.041
Uh, I was in the 1,207th class.

22:58.293 --> 23:01.004
Sir! I was in the 1,216th class, sir!

23:01.088 --> 23:03.840
What are you doing? Sit. Please sit.

23:03.924 --> 23:05.550
I will sit when you return my salute, sir.

23:05.634 --> 23:06.927
Oh, uh…

23:10.639 --> 23:11.973
So you're Marine Kim Gun-woo.

23:12.057 --> 23:13.767
- Mm.
- So which division did you serve?

23:14.351 --> 23:15.227
The First Division.

23:15.310 --> 23:17.229
Me too! Which battalion were you in, sir?

23:18.438 --> 23:20.732
- Recon.
- Amazing.

23:21.400 --> 23:24.361
I also wanted to get into reconnaissance,
but I didn't make the cut.

23:24.444 --> 23:27.072
- Mm.
- The pride of the Marines, recon.

23:27.656 --> 23:29.324
Recon! [grunts]

23:29.825 --> 23:30.700
Ah!

23:30.784 --> 23:33.453
You can still call me "bro," okay?
Let's just speak casually.

23:34.496 --> 23:35.622
I understand, sir.

23:35.705 --> 23:36.998
Yeah, but let's be casual.

23:37.082 --> 23:38.542
Casual it is, sir.

23:38.625 --> 23:39.584
Bro.

23:39.668 --> 23:40.502
Hm?

23:41.044 --> 23:41.878
Here.

23:43.422 --> 23:44.881
[both laughing]

23:44.965 --> 23:49.219
Yeah, I have a crazy amount of pride
as a marine.

23:49.302 --> 23:50.137
Why?

23:50.220 --> 23:52.681
I was kind of a thug back in Incheon,

23:52.764 --> 23:53.932
but I joined the Marine Corps,

23:54.015 --> 23:55.725
met some nice people,
and came to my senses.

23:55.809 --> 23:57.060
I just loved it all.

23:57.144 --> 24:00.856
Going through tough training together
and overcoming it all.

24:00.939 --> 24:02.274
This looks delicious.

24:02.858 --> 24:05.360
Waking up in the morning,
going on runs, sweating bullets,

24:05.444 --> 24:06.987
then showering together,

24:07.070 --> 24:09.030
washing each, all that, you know.

24:09.948 --> 24:12.451
- You're one of those crazy marines?
- Of course not.

24:12.534 --> 24:13.702
You have to try this.

24:16.288 --> 24:17.247
How is it? How is it?

24:18.165 --> 24:19.040
[exhales]

24:19.708 --> 24:21.126
It's practically steak.

24:21.209 --> 24:23.086
Really? [laughs]

24:23.670 --> 24:24.754
Let me show you something.

24:26.006 --> 24:27.215
- Watch this.
- Wow, yes.

24:27.299 --> 24:29.259
- Three pieces with ssamjang.
- Yes, yes, yes, yes.

24:29.342 --> 24:30.677
Want some kimchi with that too?

24:33.805 --> 24:34.973
Ah, ah.

24:35.056 --> 24:37.017
- Marine Kim Gun-woo, sir.
- Yeah?

24:37.100 --> 24:38.435
- [grunts]
- [grunts]

24:40.353 --> 24:41.229
Mm. Mm.

24:41.313 --> 24:43.523
- Amazing. Amazing, right?
- Uh-huh. Mm-hm

24:43.607 --> 24:44.983
- Want to get some soju?
- No.

24:45.066 --> 24:46.943
- Why? Because of your diet?
- Mm-hm.

24:47.027 --> 24:48.445
You're such a perfectionist.

24:48.528 --> 24:50.280
You're too much. [laughs]

24:50.363 --> 24:51.198
Excuse me!

24:51.698 --> 24:52.616
A beer!

24:52.699 --> 24:55.744
Please. Ah!

24:57.412 --> 24:59.080
[Gun-woo] Bro, how much were your shoes?

24:59.581 --> 25:00.999
- 1.2 mill.
- Seriously?

25:01.500 --> 25:04.169
Why so expensive?
That's a month's rent for our store.

25:04.252 --> 25:05.795
Damn, you are really gullible.

25:05.879 --> 25:07.297
Obviously they're knockoffs.

25:08.924 --> 25:10.008
Well, they look real.

25:10.550 --> 25:12.302
Knockoffs have shiny toe caps, see?

25:12.385 --> 25:13.803
And the real ones are suede.

25:13.887 --> 25:15.931
The threads around the holes
are pretty shitty too.

25:16.932 --> 25:18.141
Tell me if you wanna buy some.

25:18.225 --> 25:19.768
I can get you better than the real thing.

25:19.851 --> 25:21.853
- Really?
- Are you shitting me? No, bro.

25:21.937 --> 25:25.106
There's nothing in the world
that tops the real deal, all right?

25:26.149 --> 25:28.860
You should hang out with me more,
so we can work on your street smarts.

25:28.944 --> 25:30.779
You spend too much time
on your part-time jobs.

25:31.279 --> 25:32.113
[Woo-jin grunts]

25:33.240 --> 25:36.326
Do you know about this?
I heard it's very common these days.

25:36.409 --> 25:38.912
[groans] "COVID-19 special loans."

25:38.995 --> 25:40.330
COVID-19 SUPPORT
SUPER LOW-INTEREST SPECIAL LOAN

25:40.413 --> 25:41.540
Back in the day,

25:41.623 --> 25:45.669
I was so strapped for cash,
that I worked in money lending.

25:45.752 --> 25:47.587
Desperate people are easier to rip off.

25:47.671 --> 25:49.965
The pandemic has made
many people desperate.

25:51.091 --> 25:52.050
[Woo-jin inhales deeply]

25:52.133 --> 25:54.970
So I guess now
all the loan sharks have come out to play.

25:55.053 --> 25:55.887
Really?

25:55.971 --> 25:58.807
Since everyone is rushing
to cover their rent,

25:58.890 --> 26:01.351
all the sharks need to do
is shake their hand and suck them dry.

26:03.270 --> 26:06.565
My mom is also having a hard time
because of the rent payments for her café.

26:07.190 --> 26:09.859
The business makes less than a fourth
of what we used to,

26:09.943 --> 26:11.987
but the landlord still takes
the same amount of rent.

26:13.613 --> 26:15.865
If we close down now,
it would cost us more to move out,

26:15.949 --> 26:17.826
so we're just trying to stay afloat.

26:17.909 --> 26:20.537
Apparently, you have to return the store
to its original state.

26:21.371 --> 26:22.622
[sighs] Damn.

26:26.793 --> 26:27.627
Here.

26:29.796 --> 26:32.257
I'll treat you
to something real fancy next time.

26:33.300 --> 26:35.427
- Are we gonna have rib eye?
- Ah, just come with me.

26:35.510 --> 26:36.970
I know a good barbecue place.

26:37.053 --> 26:38.305
You aren't messing with me?

26:38.388 --> 26:42.350
Hey, do you think I would tell
such a low-level lie to a senior marine?

26:42.434 --> 26:45.395
- [chuckles] I think you would.
- So you don't believe me?

26:45.478 --> 26:47.897
I just mean
because you've been lying to me all day.

26:47.981 --> 26:50.775
- [scoffs] Man, those were just jokes.
- [chuckles]

26:50.859 --> 26:52.569
All right, I promise no more lies.

26:53.862 --> 26:55.071
- Deal.
- [chuckles]

26:55.864 --> 26:57.115
[sighs] I know.

26:57.741 --> 26:59.075
I am so sorry.

26:59.159 --> 27:00.368
I tried my best.

27:00.952 --> 27:02.454
I just couldn't… [sighs]

27:03.121 --> 27:04.748
…get it together in time.

27:05.498 --> 27:09.794
Yes, if I just get through this month,
I will come up with it somehow.

27:10.962 --> 27:12.213
Again, I am sorry.

27:13.798 --> 27:15.050
Oh, uh, sorry.

27:15.133 --> 27:17.010
- Let me call you back in the morning.
- Mom!

27:18.136 --> 27:20.263
My boy! [laughs]

27:20.347 --> 27:21.931
Oh my boy!

27:22.015 --> 27:23.266
- [Gun-woo grunts]
- [woman laughs]

27:23.892 --> 27:25.852
Look at you. You were incredible today.

27:25.935 --> 27:28.146
- You watched it?
- Oh, of course I watched it.

27:28.229 --> 27:30.940
The commentators kept talking about you
the whole time.

27:31.024 --> 27:33.777
- Are you serious?
- Yes, they kept saying you're perfect.

27:33.860 --> 27:36.363
- So I guess I should watch it too then.
- [laughs]

27:36.446 --> 27:37.489
- Mom, hold on.
- Look at you.

27:37.572 --> 27:39.199
I'm so proud of you.

27:40.200 --> 27:41.326
[Gun-woo] Here. [exhales]

27:42.202 --> 27:43.161
What's that?

27:43.870 --> 27:45.997
The prize, so we can pay the rent.

27:48.333 --> 27:49.417
Oh.

27:50.001 --> 27:51.836
Oh, no, no. I can't take this.

27:53.505 --> 27:55.423
No, Mom, I won this to give it to you.

27:56.966 --> 27:58.218
[Gun-woo laughs softly]

27:58.885 --> 28:01.888
Let's pay… Uncle back first
for what we owe.

28:02.472 --> 28:03.348
[gasps]

28:04.683 --> 28:06.601
How… how do you know about your uncle?

28:06.685 --> 28:09.979
He's also going through a lot, Mom.
Let's pay him back.

28:11.231 --> 28:12.107
[exhales]

28:14.609 --> 28:15.568
All right.

28:16.569 --> 28:19.489
But listen, I will pay you back for this
with interest.

28:19.572 --> 28:23.034
- Okay.
- Oh, thank you.

28:26.287 --> 28:29.207
- Let's go, Mom.
- Ah, it's so cold. Let's go.

28:30.333 --> 28:31.292
Did you eat?

28:31.376 --> 28:32.335
Yeah, of course.

28:32.419 --> 28:33.795
Oh, with who?

28:34.379 --> 28:35.630
The guy I fought in the finals.

28:37.507 --> 28:40.802
Oh, the boy with the curly hair?

28:40.885 --> 28:41.845
Yeah, that one.

28:42.929 --> 28:44.973
- [laughs]
- Mom, did you eat?

28:45.056 --> 28:46.516
Oh, sure, sure. I ate.

28:49.519 --> 28:50.895
[tense music playing]

29:05.201 --> 29:06.035
Sir.

29:06.619 --> 29:07.537
How are things?

29:08.413 --> 29:09.706
Sir, as you predicted,

29:09.789 --> 29:12.834
all tenants owed money to banks
or second-tier financial companies.

29:13.585 --> 29:16.629
So my plan is to bring all of them to us
by next week.

29:16.713 --> 29:19.549
Okay, can you make it happen by this week?

29:20.175 --> 29:22.969
Assemblyman Seo keeps badgering me
to kick them out quickly.

29:23.720 --> 29:25.513
[chuckles] I'll see what I can do, sir.

29:25.597 --> 29:27.724
Yes, let's hurry things along.

29:28.266 --> 29:30.268
The sales team's operations are key,
aren't they?

29:31.060 --> 29:31.895
Yes, they are.

29:36.483 --> 29:37.567
Beom, listen.

29:39.652 --> 29:40.612
Let's get ready.

29:41.905 --> 29:43.615
[tense music continues]

30:00.215 --> 30:03.301
[woman] I am team manager Yoo In-yeong
from Smile Capital.

30:03.384 --> 30:05.345
We are a financial company

30:05.428 --> 30:07.806
that was recently government-certified
for excellence,

30:07.889 --> 30:11.226
and I was wondering
if you had some time for a quick chat.

30:11.309 --> 30:12.143
Okay.

30:12.727 --> 30:15.897
Your business doesn't get many visitors
these days, huh?

30:15.980 --> 30:16.898
[sighs]

30:17.398 --> 30:18.316
No.

30:18.399 --> 30:21.152
I believe you owe the bank 40 million won.
Is that accurate, sir?

30:21.778 --> 30:22.612
Yeah.

30:22.695 --> 30:26.074
[man] Once you sign here,
we will pay off that debt today.

30:27.158 --> 30:31.412
And we have an interest rate of 5%
which is way lower than the bank's 7%.

30:31.496 --> 30:34.415
Doesn't that end up leaving you
without any actual profit?

30:34.499 --> 30:35.416
[In-yeong] That's true.

30:35.500 --> 30:38.962
But, uh, the government has started
a special support project

30:39.045 --> 30:40.880
to help the small business owners

30:40.964 --> 30:43.091
who are struggling
because of the pandemic.

30:43.174 --> 30:44.175
We won a support package,

30:44.259 --> 30:47.136
which allows us to lower interest rates
even more than the other companies.

30:47.220 --> 30:50.098
A 2% difference in interest
is not a small amount

30:50.723 --> 30:53.768
In times like these,
just staying afloat is winning.

30:54.686 --> 30:57.188
- [exhales]
- We know this pandemic will pass soon.

30:57.272 --> 30:58.523
DEBT REPAYMENT
AND NEW CONTRACT AGREEMENT

30:58.606 --> 31:01.192
But we want to extend
whatever help we can,

31:01.276 --> 31:02.777
so that you can keep your business.

31:05.363 --> 31:07.031
It's true this is good for us too.

31:07.115 --> 31:09.325
but it's really good for you, sir,

31:12.370 --> 31:14.831
- Yes, thank you.
- Thank you so much. [laughs]

31:14.914 --> 31:16.332
SMILE CAPITAL
SIGNEE YOON SO-YEON

31:22.046 --> 31:22.881
[music ends]

31:29.846 --> 31:31.514
[puffing]

31:32.557 --> 31:33.516
Huh?

31:33.600 --> 31:35.018
TEMPORARILY CLOSED
DUE TO A CONFIRMED COVID-19 PATIENT

31:35.101 --> 31:38.897
We had dinner last night
with some of the other members at the gym.

31:38.980 --> 31:40.982
Apparently, one of them tested positive.

31:42.025 --> 31:44.402
Oh, do you think I should get tested too?

31:44.485 --> 31:45.486
[coach] No, you're fine.

31:45.570 --> 31:48.364
Anyway, your match was just yesterday.

31:48.448 --> 31:50.074
Why did I hear
that you're back at the gym?

31:50.158 --> 31:52.535
- To work out. Why else?
- Gun-woo.

31:53.119 --> 31:54.329
Please take a week off and rest.

31:54.954 --> 31:56.205
Rest doing what?

31:56.289 --> 31:58.917
Nothing. If you're doing something,
you're not resting.

31:59.000 --> 32:00.752
Just don't do anything and try to relax.

32:01.502 --> 32:02.337
Okay.

32:07.216 --> 32:08.217
[sighs]

32:09.135 --> 32:12.764
[cell phone ringing]

32:12.847 --> 32:15.183
GU-NOO

32:22.941 --> 32:24.525
Uh, what are you up to?

32:24.609 --> 32:26.235
[groans]

32:26.319 --> 32:27.528
Sleep.

32:27.612 --> 32:30.031
- Huh?
- Sleeping.

32:31.157 --> 32:33.576
- Uh, I can't hear you.
- Sleep, sleeping.

32:33.660 --> 32:35.954
I am sleeping.

32:36.621 --> 32:40.291
- Well, do you want to work out?
- No.

32:40.833 --> 32:42.126
Ah, but I'm bored.

32:42.210 --> 32:45.380
God, so clingy so early in the morning.

32:45.964 --> 32:47.298
Let's hang out. Hm?

32:48.007 --> 32:49.008
[sighs]

32:50.051 --> 32:52.720
I'll send my address. Come.

32:52.804 --> 32:54.597
[chuckles] Okay, sounds good.

33:10.989 --> 33:12.031
[man] Oh shit!

33:12.782 --> 33:14.617
[woman] Fuck! Goddammit. Stop!

33:15.201 --> 33:16.452
You son of a bitch!

33:18.663 --> 33:20.456
[dramatic music playing]

33:25.086 --> 33:26.921
[panting]

33:41.185 --> 33:42.311
[sighs]

33:45.314 --> 33:46.315
[man winces]

33:47.900 --> 33:49.110
[panting]

34:01.581 --> 34:04.042
- [hesitating] Are you all right?
- [man groans]

34:04.125 --> 34:05.251
Uh, okay, wait here.

34:05.334 --> 34:07.295
[tense music playing]

34:07.378 --> 34:09.380
[panting]

34:26.689 --> 34:28.566
- [music ends]
- [Gun-woo groans]

34:29.942 --> 34:31.486
[both panting]

34:32.695 --> 34:33.529
Who?

34:33.613 --> 34:34.489
Huh?

34:35.114 --> 34:36.449
Why'd you follow me?

34:37.116 --> 34:38.242
Tell me who sent you.

34:38.326 --> 34:39.827
[groaning]

34:39.911 --> 34:42.538
[sputtering] To help.

34:42.622 --> 34:44.957
What? Help who?

34:46.209 --> 34:48.836
[spluttering]
I thought that man was being chased,

34:48.920 --> 34:50.630
and, uh, I didn't know what was going on.

34:50.713 --> 34:52.840
- God fucking dammit.
- Huh?

34:52.924 --> 34:54.717
That asshole is a fake.

34:54.801 --> 34:57.220
- [Gun-woo] Huh?
- Just butt out of things you don't know.

34:57.303 --> 34:59.764
Motherfucker. [sighs]

35:04.894 --> 35:05.728
Huh?

35:06.854 --> 35:08.314
[grunts]

35:15.905 --> 35:16.906
[exhales deeply]

35:24.997 --> 35:27.542
[doorbell rings]

35:35.174 --> 35:36.092
What brings you here?

35:36.175 --> 35:38.010
Everything went well.

35:38.094 --> 35:40.138
I mean with Mi-yeon's surgery yesterday.

35:40.221 --> 35:42.390
Oh, really? And how is she doing now?

35:42.974 --> 35:44.016
She's good, sir.

35:44.100 --> 35:46.018
She's recovering very well.

35:47.353 --> 35:48.187
[exhales deeply]

35:48.271 --> 35:49.939
It's all thanks to you.

35:50.731 --> 35:52.692
If you hadn't helped us back then, sir,

35:53.192 --> 35:55.736
my daughter might have died.

35:57.488 --> 35:58.322
[man exhales]

35:59.323 --> 36:00.158
[woman] Here.

36:02.034 --> 36:05.121
My husband had the good fortune
of moving over to a larger company,

36:05.204 --> 36:07.373
so he just received his severance.

36:08.791 --> 36:11.043
I came here
as soon as the money hit our accounts

36:11.127 --> 36:14.130
because I wanted to pay you back
before I paid anyone else.

36:14.213 --> 36:15.256
[exhales]

36:17.508 --> 36:19.218
You can take your time to pay me back.

36:20.761 --> 36:22.263
First, pay back your urgent debts.

36:22.847 --> 36:23.848
Oh, no, sir.

36:23.931 --> 36:26.475
Please. Please accept this.

36:27.268 --> 36:29.437
I finally have some peace of mind.

36:30.146 --> 36:31.355
[sobbing]

36:32.398 --> 36:33.941
Thank you so much, sir.

36:35.818 --> 36:38.362
Thank you so much. Thank you so much.

36:38.863 --> 36:40.072
[breathes deeply]

36:41.073 --> 36:43.284
Thank you. [sobbing]

36:58.799 --> 37:00.927
MI-YEON'S MOTHER APRIL 14TH, 2018
20 MILLION WON

37:01.010 --> 37:02.595
[chuckles softly]

37:06.724 --> 37:12.772
KOREAN ANTIQUE MALL

37:30.623 --> 37:31.457
[door closes]

37:32.708 --> 37:34.126
I found Yang Jae-myeong.

37:34.210 --> 37:36.629
He tried telling me he had no money,

37:36.712 --> 37:38.005
so I took this from him.

37:42.051 --> 37:43.928
This watch goes for over 20 million won.

37:44.011 --> 37:45.054
So what?

37:45.972 --> 37:48.057
Yang Jae-myeong borrowed ten million won.

37:49.058 --> 37:50.518
Yeah, plus interest.

37:50.601 --> 37:51.435
[chuckles]

37:53.896 --> 37:54.897
[exhales deeply]

37:54.981 --> 37:56.065
- [groans]
- [joints cracking]

37:56.148 --> 37:57.191
Oh, did you get hurt?

37:57.275 --> 37:59.735
[exhales] I got in a scuffle
with Yang Jae-myeong.

38:00.736 --> 38:03.239
By the way,
while we're already on the subject,

38:03.322 --> 38:04.490
you and I need to talk.

38:04.573 --> 38:05.783
Have some rice cakes first.

38:06.701 --> 38:09.161
We need to talk.
Don't try to change the subject.

38:11.539 --> 38:12.999
How long are you going to keep at it?

38:14.417 --> 38:15.251
What?

38:17.295 --> 38:19.213
Lending people money with no interest.

38:19.297 --> 38:20.965
I mean, it's not profitable.

38:21.465 --> 38:22.550
What do you mean by that?

38:22.633 --> 38:25.845
I always pay you
your 30% in commission fees.

38:25.928 --> 38:28.097
Not for me. For you, Grandpa.

38:30.516 --> 38:31.350
[inhales]

38:32.018 --> 38:33.644
You know Mi-yeon's mother?

38:34.770 --> 38:35.771
Yeah, and?

38:35.855 --> 38:39.358
She dropped by earlier
and paid back the entire sum in cash.

38:41.277 --> 38:42.361
And that's the interest?

38:44.739 --> 38:45.656
Hyeon-ju.

38:46.240 --> 38:48.909
A sick child got a timely operation
that saved her.

38:48.993 --> 38:50.536
Because I lent them money,

38:50.619 --> 38:53.664
her parents didn't have to use their home
as collateral for a loan.

38:53.748 --> 38:57.168
And now, when their child's better,
she has a home to go to.

38:58.586 --> 39:00.296
You and I saved a family.

39:01.339 --> 39:04.091
This is the most precious form of interest
in the world.

39:05.885 --> 39:06.719
[sighs]

39:07.720 --> 39:09.847
Well, anyway, I heard something

39:09.930 --> 39:12.016
while digging around
for Yang Jae-myeong's whereabouts.

39:12.892 --> 39:15.394
He and his crew are dressing up
as homeless people

39:15.478 --> 39:18.022
and robbing the actual homeless
of their IDs

39:18.105 --> 39:19.357
to take out loans in their names.

39:19.440 --> 39:21.067
And who are these people?

39:21.150 --> 39:23.319
They're not exactly the cream of the crop.

39:23.402 --> 39:24.403
They met in prison.

39:24.487 --> 39:26.447
You knew this,
and you went all by yourself?

39:27.323 --> 39:28.991
Should I have you tag along next time?

39:29.075 --> 39:31.786
- [inhales sharply]
- Anyway, let me do some digging.

39:32.453 --> 39:34.080
I think I will find something interesting.

39:34.163 --> 39:35.998
As long as you're not in danger, okay?

39:36.582 --> 39:37.458
Sure.

39:47.426 --> 39:50.471
PRESIDENT MOON GWANG-MU

39:50.554 --> 39:52.681
MARINE
IF IT DOESN'T WORK, MAKE IT WORK!

39:52.765 --> 39:53.599
Hello?

39:53.682 --> 39:56.477
Hi. Oh, is this a bad time?

39:56.560 --> 39:57.770
No, sir. No, please go ahead.

39:57.853 --> 40:00.856
Yes, I wanted to ask you a favor
to find someone.

40:00.940 --> 40:02.024
One second, please.

40:03.818 --> 40:04.819
All right, I'm listening.

40:05.903 --> 40:06.904
"A good person."

40:08.197 --> 40:09.657
"A skilled bodyguard

40:10.741 --> 40:13.285
who is familiar with the loan business."

40:16.539 --> 40:17.748
All right, sir.

40:18.249 --> 40:20.835
I will find the best candidates.
I promise I will find the best.

40:21.419 --> 40:22.753
I'll leave it in your hands.

40:22.837 --> 40:24.797
Yes, sir. Anytime.

40:26.715 --> 40:29.051
Mayweather is the top dog. No doubt.

40:29.135 --> 40:31.303
But Mayweather feels
more like a businessman

40:31.387 --> 40:32.471
than an actual boxer.

40:32.555 --> 40:33.389
That's right.

40:33.472 --> 40:36.434
My guy's in it for the money,
but he is ridiculously good at it.

40:37.143 --> 40:38.978
Probably made a few hundred billion.

40:39.520 --> 40:40.771
Does money matter to you?

40:41.897 --> 40:43.357
What could matter more than money?

40:44.066 --> 40:45.192
The heart of a boxer.

40:46.527 --> 40:47.528
[chuckles]

40:48.320 --> 40:49.196
What?

40:49.280 --> 40:51.282
[laughing]

40:51.866 --> 40:54.076
- What?
- [cackling]

40:55.995 --> 40:58.873
- Dude.
- No, No. Sorry.

41:00.082 --> 41:02.001
It's just you got so serious
all of a sudden.

41:02.084 --> 41:04.545
You looked so serious
that it really caught me off guard.

41:05.045 --> 41:06.881
Elaborate on this boxer's heart.

41:07.465 --> 41:08.340
Hm.

41:09.592 --> 41:11.927
I think Manny Pacquiao
is the best example because--

41:12.011 --> 41:15.306
Pow! Pow, pow, Pacquiao! Pow, pow.

41:15.389 --> 41:18.642
Come on, dude. Let me have my moment.
I never cut you off, man.

41:19.393 --> 41:22.605
I'm sorry, marine.
I will never cut you off. [grunts]

41:22.688 --> 41:26.942
Well, I really admire Pacquiao's heart,
you know? He never gives up.

41:27.026 --> 41:30.738
Okay, I can give him that,
but Mayweather made a lot more money.

41:30.821 --> 41:34.658
But I bet a lot more kids started dreaming
of becoming a boxer because of Pacquiao.

41:34.742 --> 41:36.160
That's true for me at least.

41:37.620 --> 41:40.539
That's the kind of person I want to be.

41:40.623 --> 41:44.168
A person who shows
that with strong will and undying passion,

41:44.251 --> 41:46.212
anyone will be able to achieve
all of their dreams.

41:46.295 --> 41:47.796
It's windy today.

41:47.880 --> 41:49.965
That is a true boxer's heart

41:50.049 --> 41:53.594
and the kind of hope we should inspire
in the people watching us.

41:54.512 --> 41:56.138
- A boxer's heart--
- Hey, this is ready.

41:56.222 --> 41:57.181
Let's eat.

41:57.264 --> 41:58.474
[inhales sharply]

41:59.350 --> 42:00.184
Here.

42:05.689 --> 42:07.399
- Is it good?
- So good.

42:08.734 --> 42:10.819
Hey, what do you do for a living?

42:10.903 --> 42:14.907
I used to teach gym classes
at a kindergarten my friend runs.

42:14.990 --> 42:16.492
[sniffles] A gym teacher of sorts.

42:17.034 --> 42:18.536
Ah, that doesn't suit you, right?

42:18.619 --> 42:19.828
What do you mean?

42:20.663 --> 42:21.830
Kids fucking love me.

42:22.414 --> 42:24.375
Well, anyway,
I used to do that in the morning,

42:24.458 --> 42:26.001
then worked out in the afternoons.

42:26.085 --> 42:27.920
Since the kindergarten shut down,
I'm in a bind.

42:30.297 --> 42:32.258
Hey, wanna go on deliveries with me?

42:32.341 --> 42:34.134
You can make some serious money
on parcel runs.

42:35.135 --> 42:36.637
- Is the pay good?
- Yeah.

42:36.720 --> 42:38.305
If we put our minds to it,

42:38.389 --> 42:40.766
we could probably make 200,000 each.

42:40.849 --> 42:41.725
For real?

42:41.809 --> 42:43.811
Yeah, delivery work is also good cardio.

42:43.894 --> 42:45.729
And you get to work on
your non-boxing muscles,

42:45.813 --> 42:47.147
so it's good for your balance too.

42:47.231 --> 42:50.651
- Ah, killing two birds with one stone.
- Three birds.

42:50.734 --> 42:51.569
Huh?

42:51.652 --> 42:54.572
You make money, get your cardio in,
and work on your balance.

42:54.655 --> 42:57.157
Yeah, cardio and balance are the same.

42:57.241 --> 42:58.993
Uh, no, they're not.

42:59.076 --> 43:00.494
[Woo-jin scoffs, clicks tongue]

43:00.995 --> 43:04.415
Wait, but aren't you supposed to compete
in the Super Series

43:04.498 --> 43:06.375
since you won
the Rookie of the Year tournament?

43:06.875 --> 43:09.795
Mm-hm, but it's been postponed
due to COVID.

43:12.298 --> 43:14.592
[sighs] How much longer?

43:15.301 --> 43:16.552
There's nothing I can do.

43:17.177 --> 43:18.012
[clicks tongue]

43:19.388 --> 43:23.142
Except I'll make sure I'm ready to fight
whenever the time actually comes.

43:26.186 --> 43:29.690
You know… you have a boxer's heart.

43:32.276 --> 43:34.361
[both laughing]

43:35.863 --> 43:38.407
- [Woo-jin puffing]
- Hm?

43:38.490 --> 43:40.367
- Come on, Pacquiao.
- Right now?

43:41.577 --> 43:42.411
[grunts]

43:46.165 --> 43:47.124
[Woo-jin groans]

43:47.207 --> 43:48.083
Whoa…

43:49.251 --> 43:50.711
Man, how could you hit me for real?

43:50.794 --> 43:52.004
Whoa, my bad. Sorry.

43:52.087 --> 43:53.547
Hey, come here, come here. Come here.

43:53.631 --> 43:54.715
Let go. Let go.

43:54.798 --> 43:57.885
- Come here. Let go. Come here. Come here.
- Whoa! Whoa!

43:57.968 --> 44:00.095
- Come here. Hey, Kim Gun-woo!
- [laughing]

44:00.971 --> 44:04.224
- [laughs] Everyone, cheers!
- [all cheering]

44:04.308 --> 44:07.603
- [electronic dance music playing]
- [all yelling]

44:07.686 --> 44:10.939
Now for today's main event.
The greatest show on Earth!

44:11.023 --> 44:13.817
- Cracking a watermelon with In-beom!
- [all cheering]

44:13.901 --> 44:17.112
Everyone, come on! Make your bets now!

44:17.196 --> 44:18.489
A million that he fails!

44:19.406 --> 44:23.243
Hey! Three million on his success.

44:24.078 --> 44:27.623
And if I'm the winner of this pot,
everything is on me!

44:27.706 --> 44:29.249
[Myeong-gil] Beom,
I know you can crack it,

44:29.333 --> 44:31.669
but I'm gonna bet four million
that you can't

44:31.752 --> 44:33.754
[all cheering]

44:33.837 --> 44:36.423
- [Jang-do chanting] Kang In-beom!
- [woman] Let's go!

44:36.507 --> 44:39.134
- Kang In-beom!
- Kang In-beom!

44:39.218 --> 44:41.178
- [yelling]
- Kang In-beom!

44:41.261 --> 44:43.013
- [In-beom grunts]
- [all cheering]

44:43.097 --> 44:43.972
He cracked it!

44:44.056 --> 44:45.933
[laughing]

44:46.016 --> 44:47.768
Tteokbokki for all! Yeah!

44:47.851 --> 44:49.645
Let's have some tteokbokki!

44:49.728 --> 44:50.813
Awesome job!

44:50.896 --> 44:51.814
Woo!

44:51.897 --> 44:53.315
I did well, didn't I?

44:53.399 --> 44:54.650
DEAREST MAYOR

44:56.902 --> 44:58.570
Shh. Quiet. Quiet!

44:58.654 --> 45:00.072
[cell phone ringing]

45:00.155 --> 45:01.532
[man clears throat]

45:05.119 --> 45:06.120
Yes, Mr. Mayor.

45:08.497 --> 45:09.832
- Yes.
- [inaudible dialogue]

45:12.626 --> 45:13.627
Yes.

45:17.673 --> 45:18.674
Yes.

45:20.175 --> 45:21.385
I understand, sir.

45:21.468 --> 45:22.761
I will let him know.

45:23.887 --> 45:25.222
Have a good evening, sir.

45:29.101 --> 45:31.770
The mayor… has just decided that

45:33.522 --> 45:34.690
he will back the casino bid.

45:35.524 --> 45:37.401
- Yes.
- Yes!

45:41.655 --> 45:43.073
[ominous music playing]

45:43.157 --> 45:48.996
I have prepared… a small gift for you,
Mr. Park, in honor of your birthday.

45:54.543 --> 45:55.377
Open it.

46:00.090 --> 46:01.884
[suspenseful music playing]

46:01.967 --> 46:03.594
Almost four kilos.

46:04.678 --> 46:09.683
Mr. Park, these gold turtles are so clean
that no one will know if you have them.

46:10.768 --> 46:12.269
I give you this with the hope

46:12.352 --> 46:15.272
that our relationship will continue
for a long time.

46:15.355 --> 46:18.692
So I would appreciate if you take them.

46:27.493 --> 46:29.870
You don't want to be in City Hall forever.

46:31.538 --> 46:33.415
I know you have big dreams, Mr. Park.

46:33.499 --> 46:36.502
If you plan on going
to the National Assembly,

46:36.585 --> 46:38.170
you will definitely need money.

46:39.129 --> 46:40.881
Let us forge a lasting partnership.

46:41.381 --> 46:43.759
I will support you every way I can.

46:45.427 --> 46:48.889
My money never has known failure.
You can rest assured.

46:50.015 --> 46:50.849
[grunts]

47:02.986 --> 47:05.864
- [slurring] Hey. Hey!
- [man] Jeez.

47:06.365 --> 47:08.367
Hey, where are we going?

47:08.450 --> 47:10.953
[man] Please get in carefully.
We'll take you home.

47:11.036 --> 47:12.496
[Mr. Park] Let's go. [grunts]

47:13.997 --> 47:14.873
[groans]

47:18.460 --> 47:20.337
And Assemblyman Seo's building?

47:21.088 --> 47:22.798
Just wait until Friday, sir.

47:23.507 --> 47:26.134
All the stores will have
over 20 million in interest.

47:26.635 --> 47:28.679
I think the small stores
need a little grilling.

47:29.179 --> 47:31.139
People tend to give up faster

47:31.223 --> 47:34.268
if they see their first-floor storefront
in complete shambles

47:34.351 --> 47:36.436
every time they come into work, you know?

47:38.272 --> 47:39.523
I'll do as you wish, sir.

47:39.606 --> 47:40.732
[Myeong-gil inhales sharply]

47:40.816 --> 47:43.485
Since Mr. Jung is not feeling well
and can't join you,

47:43.569 --> 47:46.446
call them and tell them to send over
15 intimidating men.

47:46.530 --> 47:47.990
Beom can wrap things up.

47:48.073 --> 47:49.533
Should they be armed?

47:50.117 --> 47:51.159
There's no need.

47:51.243 --> 47:54.162
Tell them to suit up
and make sure that everyone is masked.

47:54.246 --> 47:56.415
Sir, I think five men should be enough.

47:56.498 --> 47:59.459
I'm sure that the boss has his reasons.

48:01.461 --> 48:02.713
You're right.

48:03.338 --> 48:04.590
I've made a huge mistake.

48:05.090 --> 48:07.467
[both laughing]

48:07.551 --> 48:09.553
You shitheads, there you go again.

48:09.636 --> 48:11.430
Come on. Focus.

48:12.764 --> 48:13.891
Where should we begin?

48:15.601 --> 48:16.894
[exhales]

48:22.065 --> 48:23.609
[tense music playing]

48:45.213 --> 48:46.048
[music ends]

48:46.965 --> 48:48.133
[bell ringing]

48:51.219 --> 48:52.054
[So-yeon] Huh?

48:52.846 --> 48:54.848
Oh, hello. Good evening.

48:55.891 --> 48:57.184
Why didn't you keep your promise?

48:58.810 --> 48:59.645
What?

48:59.728 --> 49:01.480
You agreed to an extension fee

49:02.773 --> 49:04.608
in exchange for a lowered interest rate.

49:05.192 --> 49:06.360
Uh, what?

49:07.819 --> 49:12.658
But you needed to pay that extension fee,
which is 10% of the principal,

49:13.241 --> 49:14.868
within 24 hours of signing.

49:14.952 --> 49:16.787
- It says so on the contract.
- [gasps]

49:16.870 --> 49:18.914
But because you failed to do so,

49:19.790 --> 49:22.417
your extension
has accrued 40 million in interest.

49:22.501 --> 49:24.211
Not to mention
your credit score has dropped,

49:24.294 --> 49:26.672
so your interest rate has gone up to 20%.

49:27.297 --> 49:32.135
We really… started
with the purest of intentions.

49:32.219 --> 49:33.261
[laughs]

49:33.345 --> 49:35.347
- You ruined everything, damn it!
- [gasps]

49:35.430 --> 49:36.807
[panting]

49:37.641 --> 49:39.101
What are you going to do now?

49:40.102 --> 49:41.520
Do you have that kind of money?

49:45.232 --> 49:46.650
I will call the police.

49:47.567 --> 49:48.402
Police?

49:50.153 --> 49:51.154
Yeah.

50:00.956 --> 50:02.708
[panting]

50:02.791 --> 50:03.959
Oh my God.

50:06.670 --> 50:07.796
[phone line ringing]

50:11.133 --> 50:12.259
[Gun-woo] Hey, Mom.

50:12.342 --> 50:13.885
Hey, son, where are you?

50:13.969 --> 50:17.389
- I'm almost there.
- Okay, I'm at the store.

50:17.472 --> 50:19.558
And a bunch of strange people came over…

50:19.641 --> 50:21.435
Strange people? Who?

50:21.518 --> 50:22.602
They're still here.

50:23.562 --> 50:26.189
- [screaming]
- Mom? What's going on?

50:26.273 --> 50:27.441
[screaming]

50:33.822 --> 50:34.906
[tense music playing]

50:34.990 --> 50:37.659
[car horns honking]

50:40.287 --> 50:41.204
[grunts]

50:41.997 --> 50:44.124
- [man grunting]
- [whimpering]

50:47.419 --> 50:48.420
[music intensifying]

50:48.920 --> 50:49.796
[grunts]

50:57.596 --> 50:58.638
[Gun-woo panting]

50:59.181 --> 51:01.183
[man 1] Where the hell
do you think you're going?

51:01.266 --> 51:04.019
Who the hell are you? Get lost!

51:05.103 --> 51:07.272
Hey! I told you to scram, asshole!

51:07.856 --> 51:08.690
[So-yeon grunts]

51:09.691 --> 51:11.359
This jackass! Hey, you!

51:11.443 --> 51:13.070
[Gun-woo grunting]

51:13.153 --> 51:15.322
- [man 2] What's going on? Get him.
- [man 3] You shithead!

51:15.405 --> 51:17.074
[man 2] Who the hell is this guy?

51:19.367 --> 51:21.203
[panting]

51:23.663 --> 51:24.706
[rock music playing]

51:24.790 --> 51:26.625
[grunting]

51:30.212 --> 51:31.088
[man 5] Fuck!

51:31.171 --> 51:32.339
[grunts]

51:32.422 --> 51:33.840
- [man 6] Come here.
- [man 5] Little shit!

51:38.095 --> 51:40.514
[grunting]

52:01.451 --> 52:02.661
- [Gun-woo grunting]
- [coughing]

52:18.510 --> 52:20.053
- [shouts]
- [rock music ends]

52:21.054 --> 52:22.013
[men groaning]

52:22.097 --> 52:23.640
[So-yeon groaning]

52:23.723 --> 52:25.058
[So-yeon whimpering]

52:25.142 --> 52:27.519
- Mom, are you all right?
- Yes.

52:27.602 --> 52:28.645
You aren't hurt, are you?

52:28.728 --> 52:31.481
- [sobbing] I'm okay. I'm okay.
- [panting]

52:41.449 --> 52:42.367
Who are you?

52:43.827 --> 52:46.454
- Who are you to do this to our store?
- [grunts]

52:47.789 --> 52:49.666
- I asked you, "Who are you?"
- [grunts]

52:52.711 --> 52:54.671
- [chuckling]
- [ominous music playing]

53:04.306 --> 53:06.308
[So-yeon breathing deeply]

53:09.102 --> 53:10.437
[Myeong-gil] Calm down, kid.

53:11.396 --> 53:14.691
Your mother has borrowed some money
from our company.

53:15.275 --> 53:17.569
- [panting]
- Mm-hm

53:19.237 --> 53:20.405
So what do you want?

53:21.698 --> 53:22.908
Pay us back.

53:23.575 --> 53:25.327
Pay us for the damages first.

53:31.958 --> 53:33.960
[So-yeon whimpering]

53:44.554 --> 53:45.430
[scoffs]

53:47.098 --> 53:48.183
Go ahead.

53:53.772 --> 53:54.898
[grunts]

53:59.486 --> 54:01.863
Mom, it's okay.
Just go over there for a second.

54:01.947 --> 54:03.907
[So-yeon] Gun-woo! [whimpers]

54:03.990 --> 54:05.367
[sobbing]

54:10.830 --> 54:12.791
[music building]

54:15.252 --> 54:16.169
[Gun-woo grunting]

54:17.545 --> 54:19.172
[growls]

54:23.677 --> 54:24.511
[Gun-woo grunts]

54:26.513 --> 54:27.639
[Gun-woo grunts]

54:33.270 --> 54:34.354
[exhales]

54:36.940 --> 54:41.569
[grunting]

54:45.031 --> 54:46.491
- [In-beom grunts]
- [Gun-woo groans]

54:46.574 --> 54:47.575
[So-yeon screams]

54:48.618 --> 54:50.620
[In-beom grunting]

55:00.964 --> 55:01.798
[grunts]

55:02.632 --> 55:03.633
[grunts]

55:05.969 --> 55:06.803
[grunts]

55:12.350 --> 55:13.518
[sobbing]

55:18.356 --> 55:19.441
[grunts]

55:20.191 --> 55:21.609
[So-yeon] Gun-woo!

55:22.610 --> 55:23.611
[Gun-woo grunts]

55:23.695 --> 55:24.779
[panting]

55:27.866 --> 55:29.951
[grunting]

55:39.336 --> 55:40.503
[screams]

55:44.049 --> 55:45.050
[shouts]

55:47.969 --> 55:49.929
[In-beom grunting]

55:50.013 --> 55:51.848
Gun-woo!

55:53.350 --> 55:54.434
[grunts]

55:58.438 --> 55:59.439
[gurgles blood]

56:00.565 --> 56:01.441
[So-yeon screams]

56:10.241 --> 56:11.076
That's enough.

56:20.752 --> 56:21.669
[Myeong-gil sighs]

56:26.174 --> 56:27.717
[coughing]

56:28.802 --> 56:30.261
[So-yeon sobbing]

56:32.305 --> 56:34.933
[breathing heavily]

56:35.016 --> 56:38.978
Hey, I appreciate people with grit.

56:40.855 --> 56:44.442
Because guys with grit…
They can get anything done.

56:47.695 --> 56:49.280
Do you want to work for me?

56:49.364 --> 56:50.865
I will make sure that…

56:51.699 --> 56:52.951
[coughing]

56:55.120 --> 56:57.497
- [Gun-woo coughing]
- [scoffs]

57:03.044 --> 57:04.129
[Gun-woo gasps]

57:07.215 --> 57:08.466
[screams]

57:09.300 --> 57:10.176
[grunts]

57:10.927 --> 57:12.762
[So-yeon wailing]

57:22.355 --> 57:25.608
- [Myeong-gil grunts]
- [grunting]

57:28.027 --> 57:28.987
[grunts]

57:30.029 --> 57:32.866
[yelling]

57:36.744 --> 57:38.830
[laughing sinisterly]

57:43.209 --> 57:44.878
[theme music playing]

59:32.527 --> 59:33.695
[theme music ends]
